<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Metway year net profit falls 17 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Metway year net profit falls 17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    77.32 vs 72.33</p>
<p>    Net				     41.69 vs 50.39</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	up to 4.0 vs 12.00</p>
<p>NOTE: Metway Bank Ltd is a Queensland-based regional bank. It is about to undergo a Queensland-government sponsored merger with the Queensland Industry Development Corporation and funds management and insurance group Suncorp. Metway said a final dividend of up to 4.0 cents per share was expected to be declared before the merger was implemented.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)    up to 17.0  vs  12.0</p>
<p>    Sales				  229.83 vs 213.09</p>
<p>    Other income			  40.66 vs  36.63</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   32.78 vs  35.72</p>
<p>    Abnormal loss			 16.14 vs  nil</p>
<p>Dividend is fully franked.</p>
<p>    Tax				     24.26 vs 21.94</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  13.82 vs 14.54</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
